00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.230
Because I live in New York City commute, I'm
a high school teacher in the Bronx, and I

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.710
was wanted to get your opinion about something
because I have been.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.679
Frustrated for a few years now about the lack
of progress that comes from the Democratic

00:00:32.679 --> 00:00:37.260
Party, as far as you know, I'm a liberal minded
person, but I don't identify as a Democrat

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.460
anymore because we keep I don't want to say
losing is the wrong word, but we keep.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:50.850
Failing to pass meaningful progressive legislation,
and I think a lot of it is due to complacency,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.769
which I think comes back to something you
talk about a lot, which is lack of systematical

00:00:54.769 --> 00:00:55.769
skills.

00:00:55.769 --> 00:00:59.929
And I wanted your opinion on I see that as
a desire on both sides.

00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:04.830
And I just feel that because on the left,
we get fed more accurate information.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.440
And our media sources are generally more honest.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:11.840
Therefore, it doesn't get shown as much as
it does on the right.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.380
But I feel and this is what I want your opinion
on that because of our failing education system

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:21.670
and a lot of ways we don't have on the left,
we also lack a lot of those mixed martial

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:22.670
skills.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.420
And I'm afraid that in the future that may
come to come to the forefront in a way that's

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.620
more meaningful than it does right now.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.740
Because on the left, on the right, on the
right, obviously, it has come to the forefront.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:40.900
Speaker 1: So I think that you're not wrong
that the left sucker suckers, the left suffers

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.680
from a lack of epistemological skills, too,
to some degree.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.930
I don't think that's actually the source of
the left being ineffective in the United States.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.760
I think it's actually a lack of rhetorical
skill.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.320
I think it's it's and George Lakoff has written
about this a lot.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.260
Thomas Frank has talked about this a lot.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:05.500
We on the left, when you actually sit down
and explain to people not with a one line

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.450
slogan like if you think about the one line
slogans on abortion, right, hey, the right

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.540
is pro-life.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.590
Anything other than that is anti life.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:15.690
That's really effective.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:19.900
If you just go with a one liner, when you
really sit down with people and you explain

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.900
stuff to them, whether it's about, you know,
10 years ago when you really talked in detail

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.680
about gay marriage or you talk about health
care now or whatever the case may be, the

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.900
country is much more on the left than the
representatives that we elect.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:33.900
So what's the problem?

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.910
I don't think it's lack of a epistemological
skill.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:41.400
I think it's lack of rhetorical skill by the
left combined with and this is the other part

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.510
that's important.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:49.820
Lack of a willingness to sort of just like
power through the way that the right does

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:55.069
it, I mean, what Mitch Mitch McConnell, I
find to be a vile and immoral person, but

00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:59.630
he's essentially a Republican hero, not only
for what he's been able to get done for Republicans

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.470
over the last decade, but what he's been able
to stop Democrats from doing.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:05.459
Like, if you're a Republican, you've got to
love Mitch McConnell for what he's been able

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:06.459
to do.

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:09.590
So I think that the deficits for the Democrats
are twofold.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:15.770
One lack of rhetorical skill in talking about
these issues in ways that connect with voters

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.870
more.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:22.069
And number two, sort of a lack of willingness
to I'm not saying go low in like commit crimes

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:27.849
and do immoral things, but like get down and
really use whatever legal legal methods we

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:29.900
can use to actually get things done.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:30.980
I think those are the issues.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.200
Speaker 3: A very short while.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.540
